WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.930
Listen to two Spanish words
with almost the same spelling.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.070
hablan.

3
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:06.170
hablar.

4
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.710
The stress lands in a different place.

5
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.770
Now these: lunes.

6
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:11.790
ciudad.

7
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.350
Not one written accent among them.

8
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.730
So how does a Spanish reader know
which syllable to stress in a

9
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.350
word they've never heard?

10
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.770
In this mission, you'll learn
the two default rules that place

11
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:26.330
the stress, and see how a
written accent beats both,

12
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.370
as in teléfono.

13
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.750
Then you'll meet pairs of words
that only a small mark tells

14
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.790
apart, like "yes" and "if".

15
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.730
Your mission: find the
stress in any word,

16
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.770
and know when it needs an accent.
